This page aims to aid in progression when using {{ClassTooltip|Arcanist}} in [[Quasi-Realms#Thunderous Justice|Thunderous Justice Quasi-Realm]] by providing information, procedures, builds, or detailed recommendations.

==Quasi Tips==
* Typically a "quasi tour" involves a first pass over all of the [[Quasi-Realms]] to get them to at least 1 [[Delusion]], and depending on your [[Memories]], you can expect Thunderous Justice to get you to around 1-2 delusions from when you first hit its requirement with active play over a few days, at which point you should realm out back to prime or another quasi realm.
* The Sleight of Hand [[Paramnesics|Paramnesic]] helps slightly in this realm, but is likely not worth putting points into unless you have a lot of delusions already (at least 1 full quasi tour completed, preferably 2). You will get more profit, but probably not as much as putting that point elsewhere. If you're inclined to put points into it early anyway, only put 1 in.
* The approximate difficulty of this quasi realm to reach 5 delusions on a [[Quasi-Realms#5 Delusion Difficulty|6-scale difficulty chart]] (1 easiest, 6 hardest) is 1.

To optimise your run for 5 delusions on a subsequent pass of the quasi realm, you should have as many of the following as possible:
* The calendar [[Weekly Bonus]] should be Week of Persistence, especially later in the run.
* You should have at some point previously reached [[Mythic_Forge#Imbuement_Bonuses|paragon 46 for mythic imbuements]] and have at least one piece of gear (each) with increased stacking gain for persistent spells, augment spells, and accumulated spells (in that order of priority, but very preferably all of them).

==Attributes==
* Fill for items (Requires quite a lot - {{ItemTooltip|Blessed Tapestry}} is your friend for 1sec points)
* Important Perks
* Wis left at 240+10.
* Dom left at 0
* Rest fully cap before Vers

