Notes:
* Because we don't need to actually cast most of our memed spells except slowly in burst, we need far less shard pool than normal; 18 is enough at level 30 burst spells.
* Thanks to the increased shard pool size, it is likely you no longer need to flick between burst and the stacking set to recharge {{SpellTooltip|Jas'Aham's Thunderous Swarm|JTS}}, so you can simply stay in burst for as long as you like.
* {{SpellTooltip|Jas'Aham's Thunderous Swarm|JTS}} can benefit from a small amount of memes for cast rate (level in 2s).  The exact amount you benefit from will vary, but is unlikely to be much more than around 4. It costs a trivial amount of ink to level it to 6 and adjust its levels until you see the best cast rate.
* Spare ink can be spent on summons (5 levels at a time) for a small increase to autoclicks.